# Pin AHCI link power management to max_performance.
#
# Kernel default is `med_power_with_dipm`, which lets a SATA drive drop into a
# low-power link state. On 2026-11-15 unimatrix-02's boot SSD (Crucial MX100,
# ata2/host1) dropped off the bus mid-run: the device vanished from /sys/block,
# journald's last entry is 23:35:12 mid-line, kubelet went unreachable and sshd
# could not finish a key exchange -- while SMART still reported PASSED with 0
# reallocated / 0 pending / 0 UDMA_CRC errors and 82% life remaining. A power
# cycle brought it straight back, and no ATA link or reset event appears in any
# retained boot. DIPM is the usual suspect when a drive disappears with a clean
# SMART report, so pin every AHCI host to the highest link-power state.
#
# The 99- prefix matters: ATTR writes are last-writer-wins, and /usr/lib udev
# rules sort before /etc, so nothing distro-shipped can override this.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="scsi_host", KERNEL=="host[0-9]*", ATTR{link_power_management_policy}="max_performance"
